Subject: Re-fetch configured origins after HTTP 401 from redirected web seeds
Base: libtorrent v2.0.15
Base-Commit: 1eb18faeae156d8dbbab42935c082f8b81f50989
Apply-After: libtorrent-2.0.15-transient-webseed.patch
Apply-After: libtorrent-2.0.15-webseed-candidate-budget.patch

A redirected URL can expire after partial progress. Keep direct configured
HTTP 401 failures terminal, but let an explicitly delegated ephemeral target
schedule a fresh request to its still-enabled configured origin. Preserve
Retry-After and the native retry floor, file-specific lineage, hash bans,
manual removal, credential forwarding and IP/SSRF checks. Request snapshots
and delegation generations reject old responses and removed/re-added origins.
Fresh redirects may reuse a temporary URL without resetting banned entries.

Runtime regression: an owned origin redirects to a target that serves four
16 MiB pieces then returns 401; the origin subsequently supplies a healthy
redirect. The client must finish with a matching SHA256 without user action.
Direct configured 401, removed/stopped origins, stale generations, shared and
multi-file redirects require negative or isolation controls.

